# <repository name> — local secrets and settings. Copy this file to `.env` and fill it; `.env` is
# git-ignored and never read by Claude (.claude/settings.json denies it). Keys for
# complementary models come from the client organisation through the project lead; the
# Claude Code licence comes from the Project Advisor and needs no key here.
#
# One variable per vendor, named <VENDOR>_API_KEY (optional <VENDOR>_BASE_URL when a
# provider sits in front of several vendors). Code reads them through the project's single
# model helper, never directly. Every comment stands on its own line, above its variable.

# --- complementary models (only those a task actually needs)
# API key of one vendor
# <VENDOR>_API_KEY=
# base URL, only when a provider sits in front of that vendor
# <VENDOR>_BASE_URL=

# --- application
# Filled after the design phase, from the stack and language decision and the secrets
# decision (the twelve decisions of `design-phase` §2, #4 and #10); the names are the ones
# the "Commands" table of CLAUDE.md uses.
